<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="033" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-19 consumers — propagate per-record rights onto CallerPrincipal, delete the blanket Collaborate stamp, enforce rights on write routes</title>
    <phase>1 One evaluator</phase>
    <gate>after-032</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path .cs implementation across resolver + endpoints; tags bff-api/auth.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>FR-19 ripple through every consumer of the principal shape (orchestrator directive) — the stamp deletion changes effective rights on live routes.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies CallerPrincipalResolver.cs (orchestrator hot-file list) and ExternalCallerContext.cs shared with task 032's output.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>032</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Propagate the task-032 rights map through the caller-principal layer and the write routes. DELETE the blanket Collaborate stamp (CallerPrincipalResolver.cs — WorkforceProjectAccessLevel const at :354-360 and its application at :429-431), which today elevates a deliberate ViewOnly grant to Read|Write|Create (register A-8). After this task, a route that mutates a record must require Write from the evaluator's answer for THAT record: a View Only grant does not permit a write on any route (FR-19 acceptance).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET Minimal API + authorization filters. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>CallerPrincipal carries per-record levels for projects, matters, and work assignments sourced from AccessibleRecordSet.Rights (no blanket stamp anywhere); IAccessibleRecordSetService exposes a rights-aware check (e.g. GetRightsAsync or IsOperationPermittedAsync with a required-AccessRights argument); every /api/v1/external mutating route on scoped records requires Write via that check; unit tests cover the ViewOnly-cannot-write negative on each mutating route.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 032 made the evaluator return (recordId → rights) but consumers still flatten: WorkforcePrincipalStrategy stamps Collaborate over all accessible projects, and CallerPrincipal.AccessibleMatterIds / AccessibleWorkAssignmentIds are bare id sets. Phase 0's FR-08 task added a record-SCOPE check to PATCH /api/v1/external/todos/{id}; this task upgrades scope-membership to rights-aware enforcement. CiamContactPrincipalStrategy already carries per-project levels from grants — extend the same fidelity to matters/WAs on both planes.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalCallerContext.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetServiceTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/Tier2ScopeFilterInjector.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="032" status="pending">The rights map on AccessibleRecordSet + level→rights mapping.</dependency>
      <dependency task="Phase 0 FR-08 task (see TASK-INDEX)" status="pending">The record-scope check on PATCH /api/v1/external/todos/{id} that this task upgrades to rights-aware. If it has not landed, implement the rights-aware check directly (it subsumes the scope check) and note it.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 (as amended by task 030)">Scope: all enforcement added here. Decisions come from the ONE evaluator (AccessibleRecordSetService) — do not re-derive rights in endpoints, do not consult grant rows directly from a route handler.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Scope: route enforcement. Record-level authorization on external routes stays in endpoint filters / explicit per-endpoint checks — no global middleware.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec NFR-01">Scope: every path touched. A record absent from the rights map, an unresolved principal, or a faulted compose DENIES the mutation (403) — never falls through to the write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the stamp deletion. Remove WorkforceProjectAccessLevel and its .Select(...) application entirely — grep the repo for WorkforceProjectAccessLevel afterwards and assert zero references. Do NOT reintroduce any per-plane default level; every level flows from AccessibleRecordSet.Rights.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: read routes. Read-path behavior (scope injection via id sets, module predicates, GetAccessible*Ids) must be unchanged in this task — only mutating routes gain the Write requirement.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR (BFF-touching). State the placement decision citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md; run dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/ and report compressed size + diff vs ~44.96 MB baseline; ceiling 60 MB (NFR-06).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>caller-principal composition, endpoint authorization</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-003-authorization-seams.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/design-register.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="deny mapping" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs">WorkforcePrincipalStrategy's 401/403 ProblemDetails mapping with reasonCode extensions is the deny-shape to reuse for insufficient-rights (403 + machine-readable code).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL. Read CallerPrincipalResolver.cs end-to-end, ExternalCallerContext.cs (CallerPrincipal, CallerProjectAccess, GetAccessible*Ids), and enumerate every mutating /api/v1/external route (grep MapPatch/MapPost/MapPut/MapDelete under Api/ExternalAccess/).</step>
    <step order="1">Extend CallerPrincipal so matters and WAs carry per-record levels (mirroring ProjectAccess) while GetAccessibleMatterIds/GetAccessibleWorkAssignmentIds keep returning id sets for scope injection.</step>
    <step order="2">WorkforcePrincipalStrategy: source per-record levels from AccessibleRecordSet.Rights for all three root types; DELETE the blanket stamp const + application. CiamContactPrincipalStrategy: carry matter/WA levels from the task-032 grant set.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the rights-aware check to IAccessibleRecordSetService (required-rights argument, fail-closed) and wire it into every mutating route found in step 0 — at minimum the external To Do PATCH. Enumerate the wired routes in the PR description.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: per-route ViewOnly-denied / Collaborate-allowed pairs; principal-shape tests for matter/WA levels; grep-assertion that WorkforceProjectAccessLevel is gone.</step>
    <step order="5">Build + full unit test run; publish-size measurement per §10.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation (incl. the exact mutating-route inventory) in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a mutating external route exists whose record cannot be resolved to a scoped root (no entityType/recordId to evaluate), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the route list — do not ship it unguarded and do not invent a scope for it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If deleting the blanket stamp visibly REDUCES rights for a live legitimate flow other than the intended ViewOnly demotion (e.g. systemusers writing to membership-derived records would lose Write because membership now maps below Collaborate), STOP — that indicates a term-level regression against task 032's status-quo constraint.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalCallerContext.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetServiceTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a contact whose ONLY source on project P is a ViewOnly grant, PATCH /api/v1/external/todos/{id} for a todo under P returns 403 with a machine-readable reason code (FR-19 acceptance: a View Only grant does not permit a write on any route).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same caller holding Collaborate on P, the same PATCH succeeds (positive control).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">CallerPrincipal carries per-record levels for projects, matters, and work assignments; a matter-granted-Collaborate + matter-granted-ViewOnly caller shows the two different levels (no flattening).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: grep for WorkforceProjectAccessLevel returns zero hits; no other constant supplies a blanket per-plane level.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a record absent from the composed rights map is denied (403) on every wired mutating route — covered per route.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Read-path regression: existing module-scope injection tests and GetAccessible*Ids behaviors pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; publish size reported and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-19 + register A-8. The mutating-route inventory produced in step 0 is load-bearing for review — include it verbatim in the PR. Coordinate with Phase 0's FR-07 delegation task (grant/revoke endpoints get their own Write-on-target check there; do not duplicate it here).

COMPLETED 2026-09-04. Full record: notes/task-033-consumer-propagation.md.

Key finding, which reframed the task: the Create/Write gates on all four mutating routes ALREADY EXISTED. They could not fire because the workforce plane blanket-stamped Collaborate, so GetEffectiveRights returned Read|Create|Write regardless of the grant row. The deliverable was making the existing gates TRUE, not adding gates.

Deviation from step 3 (steps are mode="directional"): IAccessibleRecordSetService.IsOperationPermittedAsync was ADDED as required, but the four routes are wired through CallerPrincipal's rights rather than by calling it per route. The principal already carries the SAME evaluator answer, composed once at resolve time; calling the service per route would re-compose the whole accessible set and cost a second Dataverse round trip for data already in hand. Both read the one evaluator, so they cannot drift. The new method remains the seam for callers that have no CallerPrincipal (e.g. the workforce download gate).

Escalation triggers: BOTH checked, NEITHER fired. (1) No unguarded mutating route — 12 Map* sites: 4 scoped (gated here), 7 on adminGroup behind DelegationRuleFilter (FR-07's surface), 1 is a POST-bodied READ. (2) No term-level regression — MembershipTermRights is byte-identical to Collaborate, so membership-derived flows keep their rights.

Additional scope taken, deliberately: the matter/work-assignment "membership implies write" asymmetry was removed (it was documented in the handler as intentional, but tasks 032/033 removed its premise), and ADR-003's machine-readable-deny-code MUST was applied to the three POST gates that lacked one.

Verified: suite 12,074 passed / 0 failed; ArchTests 191/191; publish delta 0.00 MB vs a FRESH master build (45.46 MB both sides); no vulnerable packages; `grep WorkforceProjectAccessLevel` = 0. The single merged guard was perturbation-tested — removing it fails 11 of 19 ExternalTodoScopeTests.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
